        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f0833de3-f70e-50ec-8119-3ac6fc76c2b8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Walt Disney, Esther Forbes, Hal Stalmaster, Elijah Isaacs\n- Companies: Walt Disney Productions, WED Enterprises\n- Products: Johnny Tremain, Magic Kingdom, Disneyland Park\n- Places: Boston, Massachusetts, Anaheim, California, Wilkes County, North Carolina\n- Events: American Revolution\n\nFacts:\n- Esther Forbes wrote the children's novel Johnny Tremain, which won the Newbery Medal in 1944.\n- In 1957, Walt Disney Productions made the film Johnny Tremain, based on Esther Forbes's novel and set in Boston, Massachusetts before the outbreak of the American Revolution.\n- Hal Stalmaster, born Harry Lapidus Stalmaster on March 29, 1940, is an American former actor known for the lead role in the 1957 Walt Disney film Johnny Tremain.\n- Magic Kingdom was initialized by Walt Disney and designed by WED Enterprises, and its layout and attractions were based on Disneyland Park in Anaheim, California.\n- Magic Kingdom is dedicated to fairy tales and Disney characters.\n- Elijah Isaacs, who lived from about 1730 to 1799, was an early farmer, statesman, and militia officer in Wilkes County, North Carolina during the American Revolution.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "949bf89c-2238-57b4-90ce-906829fd90a9",
        "text": "Page: Johnny Tremain (film). Sentence: Johnny Tremain is a 1957 film made by Walt Disney Productions, based on the 1944 Newbery Medal-winning children's novel of the same name by Esther Forbes, retelling the story of the years in Boston, Massachusetts prior to the outbreak of the American Revolution.\nPage: Magic Kingdom. Sentence: Initialized by Walt Disney and designed by WED Enterprises, its layout and attractions are based on Disneyland Park in Anaheim, California, and is dedicated to fairy tales and Disney characters.\nPage: Hal Stalmaster. Sentence: Harry Lapidus Stalmaster, known as Hal Stalmaster (born March 29, 1940), is an American former actor, known for his lead role in the 1957 Walt Disney film of the American Revolution \"Johnny Tremain\", based on the 1943 Esther Forbes novel of the same name.\nPage: Elijah Isaacs. Sentence: Elijah Isaacs (173?\nPage: Elijah Isaacs. Sentence: -1799) was an early farmer, statesman, and militia officer in Wilkes County, North Carolina during the American Revolution.",
